        "verdict": "PASS",
        "reasons": "NO_PLAN is correct and names a true constraint, not missing evidence. Recomputed: $2,000 / $300 = 6.67, so 7 orders; 7 x 5 owner hours (card humanHours=5; fulfillmentOwner = the owner personally) = 35 h, against 3 h/week x 4 weeks = 12 h. 12 h fulfils floor(12/5)=2 orders = $600. Even with all 8 signed orders evidenced, the owner-hours limit cannot be met, so the gap is a constraint. No alternative fulfiller is on record, so subcontracting cannot be assumed. Price is real signed buyer orders, cost $0, settlement 7 days within 28, so no other link is the decisive one.",
        "findings": [
          "Arithmetic verified: 7 deals x 5 h = 35 h > 12 h ceiling; 2 deals = $600 fit.",
          "Brain's own check reports 40 h (all 8 agreed deals); the revision's 35 h (minimum 7 deals) is the correct minimum to reach target and the conclusion is the same.",
          "Resolution options (raise hours to ~9/week, lower target to $600, or record a drafter) are coherent; note 35 h/4 weeks = 8.75 h/week and that selling/collection time would add to it."
        ],
